Transformation notes (abstract)
- Time mapping
  - WebVTT: use tb-media seconds with millisecond precision; cues begin/end = segment intervals; merge lock-step segments according to cuePolicy.
  - IMSC: use clock-time expressions or frames; regions mapped to tt:region; styles mapped to tt:style; spans become tt:p children with tt:br for explicit breaks.
- Flow to target
  - Regions translate to target-specific positional constructs; linePacking emits explicit break marks or splits into multiple cues if required.
- Styles
  - Abstract style ids are mapped to target classes or style elements; declarations are translated only if supported by the target.
- Validation
  - Ensure no overlapping cues unless allowed by the target; resolve collisions via stacking and region overflow policies; enforce time precision limits.

This schema enables consistent, platform-neutral authoring and transformation of segmented textual data with hierarchical structure, synchronized timing, and deterministic layout across multiple interfaces and formats.

